album from 10 plus years ago that we miss dearly uh it's my pick today so i have the fiery furnaces bitter tea album um the fiery furnaces is a brother sister duo formed in brooklyn new york in like the early 2000s um and i just really like this album because it's really springy uh and it's very like experimental and silly and i feel like it's a good testament that you don't need like ableton 3000 plus to be able to make like really fun um clever music and i think being a brother and sister duo kind of gives way to um like a sound that maybe couldn't be conceived without that connection um yeah so coming up is black hearted boy from the fiery furnaces you're in 704 Die!"}, {"start": "00:18:45", "end": "00:19:08", "text": ""}, {"start": "00:28:39", "end": "00:29:31", "text": "Hey, it's Rhea. You're listening to 704 W High St on FBi Radio 94.5. I am coming to you from the streets of Melbourne after having chosen my I Miss You for this week. And the album that I chose is the 2007 album Boxer by The National. I got thinking about this album on this trip after hearing rumours of the modern baseball reunion. I'm not sure if that's still happening or if that was ever in the works. but regardless um their amoeba records video what's in my bag video was very formative to me and i'm pretty sure that boxer was one of the chosen records featured in that video um and it's such a great album but you'll be finding that out very soon um yeah here it is"}, {"start": "00:39:31", "end": "00:39:50", "text": "I know somebody sleep on me that don't rock the way that I wrote, eh, rock the way that I wrote, I know somebody sleep on me that don't rock the way that I wrote, when you got up and up to me, I been knocking on your door, I, I, I really been dealing with you."}, {"start": "00:44:03", "end": "00:45:10", "text": "Hey, you're listening to 704 W High St on FBi Radio 94.5. I played you some new Bootleg Baby and some new Eyes of Zatu, both collaborations. The Eyes of Zatu track was I Don't Gotta Tell Nobody and Bootleg Baby was Done Is Done. And before that, I played for you some of The National. Please go check out the track list on our programs page. It's such a good album. um but i have more for you and i've also been interested in the they're getting a body of water album that came out maybe maybe it was mid mid this month oh sorry mid last month now that it's november um but there's some crazy features there's hooky there's a country uh a country western there's tony bontana there's cooper b handy and those are just a handful of the features on the album so go check it out but in the meantime this is my happening by their guarding a body of water featuring featuring spirit of the beehive"}, {"start": "00:56:19", "end": "00:56:58", "text": "Hey, this is Pat. You're listening to 704 W High St on FBi Radio 94.5. All of the tracks I'm about to play for you are by artists that performed over the last few days at Sore Horse Festival in Melbourne. I had the honour of attending both nights and saw some amazing bands, some I'd seen before, a few I'd long wanted to see, but had a fantastic time. Huge congrats to Benji and the Sore Horse community on putting on such an amazing festival. This first track is by Sydney band Half Request off of their upcoming EP. The song is called Dog Puck. You're on FBA."}, {"start": "01:23:57", "end": "01:24:33", "text": "Hey, this is Pat. You're listening to 704 W High St on FBi Radio 94.5. All the tracks you've just heard over the last little while were by artists who performed at Saw Horse Festival at the Tote in Melbourne over the last couple of days. The one just then was Sliding Doors by DS Heavy. And before that, Fruit to Right by Twine, The Feeling Remains by Our Mutual Friend, definitely a sing-along crowd favourite. And before that, Doggy Dog World by Awnings, who were fantastic to see live. Really cool math rock band. And anyway, make sure you hang around. Peter Hollow is up next on Utility 4."}, {"start": "01:40:16", "end": "01:40:47", "text": "Hey, this is Mona coming at you with a rare pre-recorded message on 704, because the whole team is still in Melbourne right now, preceding our Melbourne birthday show at Miscellanea. You just heard another two songs from artists who performed, Friday Night by Amanda and W Life by Synergy Trilogy. If you stick around, you'll catch Utility Fog by Peter Hollow. Just going to play a couple more tracks for you to finish off the night. This is 704. You"}, {"start": "01:57:29", "end": "01:58:10", "text": "Right there was Brain Freeze by Riff Raff, sped up a little sample from Mr. Celia Hart's DJing, one of the best producers in Australia, and who delivered one of the most turnt DJ sets I think I've ever seen at our miscellaneous show. um just want to finish off the night with uh something that was very special to us as we were traveling this is don't worry by drake as performed by earl sweatshirt and mike at miscellanea closing their australian tour last year"}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:00:00"}, "track": {"title": "Mariner's Apartment Complex", "artists": [{"name": "Prophetic Justice Ministry"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:05:12"}, "track": {"title": "Ufon Taxi", "artists": [{"name": "Nick Asaya"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:06:47"}, "track": {"title": "Party Dress", "artists": [{"name": "Felicity J Lord"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:10:07"}, "track": {"title": "Chaos", "artists": [{"name": "Amanda"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:15:37"}, "track": {"title": "Black-Hearted Boy", "artists": [{"name": "The Fiery Furnaces"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:26:00"}, "track": {"